{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:c8e08910503a3e10","name":"Jedi Sage Master","source":{"id":"source:reference-c8e08910503a3e10","title":"Jedi Sage Master","revision":25219,"timestamp":"2024-11-13T20:05:41Z","sha256":"96afa3b366bfdeec9b359220a669185ab1f2f561380e4c20774e4127a08843b4","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=25219","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Jedi%20Sage%20Master&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-c8e08910503a3e10","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Some Jedi Masters are known as scholars even among their peers. These individuals, sometimes called Jedi Sage Masters, are the keepers of knowledge, and they spend much of their time deep in research or contemplation. They seek to test the boundaries of what is possible, while at the same time passing on this knowledge to those around them. If a question or problem comes to light that cannot be answered by members of the Jedi Council, these scholars are consulted.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Though they are seldom seen outside the walls of the Jedi Temple on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"},", Jedi Sage Masters do sometimes venture out in order to conduct field research. This research might involve the excavation of a Sith Temple or the observation of a new ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"}," or life form. Keeping the archives up to date requires a constant influx of information. Jedi scholars and their apprentices, along with non-Jedi experts, are at the forefront of this never ending process.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Jedi Sage Masters are often asked to meet with potential Padawan learners in order to judge their Force potential. In this regard, they uphold their duty to help teach new Jedi by discerning which students have the most aptitude with ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},". They often take on Padawans of their own, especially if a candidate is intellectually adept and eager to learn more mundane abilities.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Although the Jedi Sage Master detailed in this entry is an expert in Galactic Lore as well as Physical and Life Sciences, Jedi scholars are a diverse group. The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knowledge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knowledge","referenceId":"reference:dcb3e1c00e79236d"}," skills in this statistics block can be replaced with any other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knowledge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knowledge","referenceId":"reference:dcb3e1c00e79236d"}," specialty. Given their knowledge of customs and philosophical thought, scholars who specialize in the Social Sciences often excel in a consular role, while those who focus on Tactics might serve as generals among ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["The Presence of a Master"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The rank of Master is conferred on Jedi who prove themselves to be not only excellent teachers, but true masters of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},". Though not every Master becomes a member of the Jedi Council, Jedi Masters are regarded as the ultimate authority on matters concerning ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},". The presence of a Jedi Master should be a momentous event in a campaign, because a Master's wisdom and knowledge is usually unparalleled. Even experienced Jedi Knights who have years of service under their belts pause to show a Jedi Master the proper respect, and those who come to the rank at a young age (such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Obi-Wan Kenobi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Obi-Wan_Kenobi","referenceId":"reference:6e84377ee76928db"},") are both rare and revered.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Including a Jedi Master in your campaign can cause some problems if not properly handled. For one, the heroes might come to rely on the power that a Jedi Master wields if the Master spends much time accompanying them. Similarly, some heroes might think they can use the Jedi Master to solve all their problems, calling upon the Master's knowledge and experience even for the most trivial matters. Finally, some players might feel as though their heroes are outshined by a prominent Jedi Master appearing in the campaign, and they could come to resent the Master as a character much more powerful than their own.\n"]},"\n","\n\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Jedi Sage Master Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Even though a Jedi Sage Master is somewhat less combat-oriented than their peers, this does not mean they should be trifled with. Though they are sometimes typified as stodgy old codgers with their noses buried in old ",{"tag":"a","children":["Holocrons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Holocrons","referenceId":"reference:78fdd3622bfea307"},", Jedi Sage Masters are some of the most powerful members of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi Order"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi_Order"},". The knowledge that they possess on an individual basis is staggering, and they can call upon the lessons of the past in order to solve the problems of the future.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["In combat, a Jedi Sage Master concentrates on self-defense and disarming an opponent. Negotiation is an important component of their strategy, and they are not above using ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," in order to facilitate a peaceful resolution to a potentially dangerous situation.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Jedi Sage Master Statistics (CL 15)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId":"reference:0b0e48747027a29d"}," 7/",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Knight"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Knight","referenceId":"reference:8a1e23d924066b37"}," 5/",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Master"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Master","referenceId":"reference:5fac760c8a2485ba"}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Destiny Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Destiny_Points"},":"]}," 1; ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 6\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +8, ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Foresight"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Foresight"}]},"; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Improved Sense Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Improved_Sense_Force","referenceId":"reference:8f3ced475f793949"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use the Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_the_Force","referenceId":"reference:74883d1dd46b87fe"}," +19\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, 7 Unassigned